{"format":"kards-original-reference","version":1,"id":"640089015bd4d92e","name":"card_unit_15th_recon_regiment","package":"/Game/Blueprints/Cards/Britain/CovertOp/units/card_unit_15th_recon_regiment","parent":"UBaseCardObject","card":{"title":"15th RECCE","text":"Deployment: Target a unit. \r\n15th RECCE gets +1+1 and Guard when the targeted unit deals damage.","flavorText":"The 15th Scottish Reconnaissance Regiment was a unit of the 15th (Scottish) Infantry Division, active during WWII. The division was formed in 1939 as part of the Territorial Army and it remained in the United Kingdom for training and home defense duties. In June 1944, they landed in Normandy shortly after D-Day and participated in Operation Epsom and the capture of Caen as part of the British 21st Army Group. They continued to fight through France, Belgium, and the Netherlands, where they participated in Operation Veritable and Operation Plunder. The 15th (Scottish) Infantry Division was disbanded on April 10th, 1946, after suffering over 11,000 casualties, including over 1,500 killed in action over 11 months of fighting. The division was highly regarded and considered one of the best-led infantry divisions in the 21st Army Group.","faction":"Britain","type":"infantry","rarity":"Uncommon","cost":3,"operationCost":1,"attack":3,"defense":3},"defaults":{"UberGraphFrame":{},"Name":"card_unit_15th_recon_regiment","title":{"Namespace":"card_britain","Key":"card_unit_15th_recon_regiment_title","SourceString":"15th RECCE","LocalizedString":"15th RECCE"},"Type":"ETypeEnum::infantry","attack":3,"defense":3,"range":1,"faction":"EFactionEnum::Britain","kredits":3,"Text":{"Namespace":"card_britain","Key":"card_unit_15th_recon_regiment_text","SourceString":"Deployment: Target a unit. \r\n15th RECCE gets +1+1 and Guard when the targeted unit deals damage.","LocalizedString":"Deployment: Target a unit. \r\n15th RECCE gets +1+1 and Guard when the targeted unit deals damage."},"flavorText":{"Namespace":"card_britain","Key":"card_unit_15th_recon_regiment_history","SourceString":"The 15th Scottish Reconnaissance Regiment was a unit of the 15th (Scottish) Infantry Division, active during WWII. The division was formed in 1939 as part of the Territorial Army and it remained in the United Kingdom for training and home defense duties. In June 1944, they landed in Normandy shortly after D-Day and participated in Operation Epsom and the capture of Caen as part of the British 21st Army Group. They continued to fight through France, Belgium, and the Netherlands, where they participated in Operation Veritable and Operation Plunder. The 15th (Scottish) Infantry Division was disbanded on April 10th, 1946, after suffering over 11,000 casualties, including over 1,500 killed in action over 11 months of fighting. The division was highly regarded and considered one of the best-led infantry divisions in the 21st Army Group.","LocalizedString":"The 15th Scottish Reconnaissance Regiment was a unit of the 15th (Scottish) Infantry Division, active during WWII. The division was formed in 1939 as part of the Territorial Army and it remained in the United Kingdom for training and home defense duties. In June 1944, they landed in Normandy shortly after D-Day and participated in Operation Epsom and the capture of Caen as part of the British 21st Army Group. They continued to fight through France, Belgium, and the Netherlands, where they participated in Operation Veritable and Operation Plunder. The 15th (Scottish) Infantry Division was disbanded on April 10th, 1946, after suffering over 11,000 casualties, including over 1,500 killed in action over 11 months of fighting. The division was highly regarded and considered one of the best-led infantry divisions in the 21st Army Group."},"operationCost":1,"rarity":"ERarityEnum::Uncommon","selectTargetOnPlayedFromHand":true,"cardSet":"ECardSetEnum::CurrentExpansion","isReserved":true,"EffectType":"ECardEffectTypes::Trigger","usedTriggers":["ERegisteredCardFunc